Represents one component or raw material inside a Bill of Materials, defining the exact quantity, unit, and consumption rules needed to produce the parent product.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Define raw materials, sub-assemblies, and consumables in BOMs
Support multi-level BOM explosion
Control flexible vs strict consumption during production
Manage by-products / co-products (via byproduct_id)
Calculate component requirements for Manufacturing Orders
Support product variants and optional components

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent)
Key Fields:
bom_id → mrp.bom (required, parent)
product_id → product.product (required)
product_qty (float), product_uom_id
type (normal / phantom)
operation_id (link to specific workcenter operation)
bom_id (sub-BOM for multi-level)
consumption (flexible / strict / warning)
sequence, active

Critical Hooks: _bom_explode, onchange_product_id, _compute_total_cost
Security: Inherited from parent BOM (mrp.group_mrp_manager)

RAG Routing Keywords:
BOM line, BOM component, bill of material line, component quantity, raw material line, mrp.bom.line, BOM explosion, production component, material consumption, sub BOM, phantom component
Related Models (most joined):

mrp.bom (parent)
product.product / product.template
mrp.production (via BOM explosion)
mrp.workorder
stock.move (generated consumption moves)
uom.uom

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
mrp.bom.line is the child model of mrp.bom that stores each component with product_id, product_qty, uom, consumption mode (flexible/strict), operation_id, and sub-bom reference. It drives BOM explosion, material requirement calculation, consumption during manufacturing orders, costing, and multi-level production structures in Odoo MRP.